><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Kulisevsky</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Deus</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Junque</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Pujol</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Guardia</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Neuropsychological alterations in patients with computed tomography-detected basal ganglia calcification</article-title><source>Arch Neurol</source><year>1996</year><volume>53</volume><fpage>251</fpage><lpage>256</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8651878</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Benke</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Karner</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Seppi</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Delazer</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Marksteiner</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Donnemiller</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Subacute dementia and imaging correlates in a case of Fahr's disease</article-title><source>J Neurol Neurosurg Psychiatry</source><year>2004</year><volume>75</volume><fpage>1163</fpage><lpage>1165</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15258221</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Saver</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>GT</given-names></name><name><surname>Charness</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Idiopathic striopallidodentate calcification with prominent supranuclear abnormality of eye movement</article-title><source>J Neuroophthalmol</source><year>1994</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>29</fpage><lpage>33</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8032477</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Galvez-Jimenez</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Hanson</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name><name><surname>Cabral</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Dopa-resistant parkinsonism, oculomotor disturbances, chorea, mirror movements, dyspraxia, and dementia: the expanding clinical spectrum of hypoparathyroidism. A case report</article-title><source>Mov Disord</source><year>2000</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>1273</fpage><lpage>1276</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11104223</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Calabrese</surname><given-names>VP</given-names></name><name><surname>Hadfield</surname><given-names>MG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Parkinsonism and extraocular motor abnormalities with unusual neuropathological findings</article-title><source>Mov Disord</source><year>1991</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>257</fpage><lpage>260</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1922131</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Litvan</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Agid</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Calne</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Campbell</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Dubois</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Duvoisin</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Clinical research criteria for the diagnosis of progressive supranuclear palsy (Steele-Richardson-Olszewski syndrome): report of the NINDS-SPSP international workshop</article-title><source>Neurology</source><year>1996</year><volume>47</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8710059</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lowe</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Lennox</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Leigh</surname><given-names>PN</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Graham</surname><given-names>DI</given-names></name><name><surname>Lantos</surname><given-names>PL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Disorders of movement disorders and system degenerations</article-title><source>Green-field's Neuropathology</source><year>1997</year><volume>Vol II</volume><edition>6th edn</edition><publisher-loc>London</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Arnold</publisher-name><fpage>281</fpage><lpage>366</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bronsky</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Kushner</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name><name><surname>Dubin</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Snapper</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Idiopathic hypoparathyroidism and pseudohypoparathyroidism: case reports and review of the literature</article-title><source>Medicine</source><year>1958</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>317</fpage><lpage>352</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">13621989</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nath</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Ben-Shlomo</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomson</surname><given-names>RG</given-names></name><name><surname>Morris</surname><given-names>HR</given-names></name><name><surname>Wood</surname><given-names>NW</given-names></name><name><surname>Lees</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The prevalence of progressive supranuclear palsy (Steele-Richardson-Olszewski syndrome) in the UK</article-title><source>Brain</source><year>2001</year><volume>124</volume><fpage>1438</fpage><lpage>1449</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11408338</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vaamonde</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Legarda</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Jimenez-Jimenez</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Zubieta</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Obeso</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Levodopa-responsive parkinsonism associated with basal ganglia calcification and primary hypoparathyroidism</article-title><source>Mov Disord</source><year>1993</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>398</fpage><lpage>400</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8341314</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hempel</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Henze</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Berghoff</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Garcia</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Ody</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Schroder</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>PET findings and neuropsychological deficits in a case of Fahr's disease</article-title><source>Psychiatry Res</source><year>2001</year><volume>108</volume><fpage>133</fpage><lpage>140</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11738547</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hikosaka</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Takikawa</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Kawagoe</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Role of the basal ganglia in the control of purposive saccadic eye movements</article-title><source>Physiol Rev</source><year>2000</year><volume>80</volume><fpage>953</fpage><lpage>978</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10893428</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><fig id="F1" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Computed tomography (CT) of the brain demonstrated extensive, bilateral calcification of the basal ganglia, centrum semiovale, and bilateral dentate nuclei of the cerebellum (A). Magnetic resonance imaging revealed mixed high- and low-intensity signals compatible with the distribution of calcification on CT. The red nucleus and substantia nigra appeared normal (B).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jcn-3-57-g001"/></fig><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>The neuropsychological findings of the patient</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jcn-3-57-i001"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>N; Normal, K-BNT; Korean-version Boston Naming Test, Rey-CFT; Rey-Osterrieth Complex Figure Test</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>